# 0001 — the vendored samples type in the kit's face, not the platform default.
#
# Every `@Preview` here is upstream's own, and its body opens with a bare `GlimmerTheme { }` as the
# OUTERMOST composable. A stock `GlimmerTheme()` types in the platform default — Roboto on this
# Robolectric lane — so the whole sheet published in the wrong face while `:glimmer-catalog`, which
# applies `createGoogleSansFlexTypography()` in its own `Sticker` wrapper, published correctly.
#
# It is invisible from inside the module: the samples are faithful to upstream, nothing fails, and
# the 2026-09-16 Google Sans Flex renderer fix (compose-preview-daemon#114) moved 52 files in
# `:glimmer-catalog` and not one byte here — there was no Google Sans Flex in this module to fix.
# A designer comparing this sheet against the kit is comparing the wrong typeface, which is the
# defect `:glimmer-catalog`'s own KDoc describes as scoring components "against the kit in the
# wrong face".
#
# The substitution is mechanical and the sample BODIES are untouched: `@Preview` becomes
# `@GlimmerSamplePreview`, this module's multi-preview annotation, which carries the same `@Preview`
# plus `@PreviewWrapperClass(GoogleSansFlexPreviewWrapper)`. The wrapper supplies the typography
# from outside, and the sample's own inner `GlimmerTheme { }` INHERITS it rather than overriding it,
# because `GlimmerTheme`'s `typography` parameter defaults to the ambient `GlimmerTheme.typography`
# — verified against glimmer-1.0.0-alpha19.aar, whose default branch calls
# `GlimmerTheme$Companion.getTypography`, which reads `_localGlimmerTheme.current.typography`.
#
# Preview ids derive from the function, not the annotation, so nothing downstream moves:
# `glimmer-design-map.json`, the parity references and the published slugs are unchanged.
